<BaseLayout title="Concept Overview" description="Conceptual overview of AdaptiveCAD and Adaptive Pi geometry">
  <h1>AdaptiveCAD Concept Overview</h1>
  <p class="meta">Foundations of πₐ (Adaptive Pi) Geometry</p>
  <p>AdaptiveCAD is built on the revolutionary concept of "Adaptive Pi Geometry" (πₐ), a curvature-first approach where curves—not straight lines—are the fundamental primitive objects.</p>

  <h2>Core Principles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Curvature-First Design:</strong> Curves are the fundamental primitives, reflecting physical reality where no perfect straight lines exist.</li>
    <li><strong>Adaptive Pi (πₐ) Geometry:</strong> Dynamic metric tensor allowing location-dependent curvature for more realistic modeling.</li>
    <li><strong>Manufacturing Alignment:</strong> CAD models naturally align with manufacturing toolpaths and processes.</li>
    <li><strong>Parametric Control:</strong> Precise control over curve properties including curvature, torsion, and continuity.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Mathematical Foundation</h2>
  <pre><code>// Dynamic metric tensor
g_ij(p,t) = metric at point p and parameter t
ds² = g_ij dx^i dx^j

// Constraint-driven curvature update  
∂g_ij/∂t = -α ∂Φ/∂x^i ∂Φ/∂x^j

// Geodesic computation for toolpaths
ẍ^k + Γ^k_ij ẋ^i ẋ^j = 0</code></pre>

  <h2>Applications</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Advanced parametric shape creation (Superellipse, Pi Curve Shell, Helix)</li>
    <li>Curvature-aware toolpath generation for manufacturing</li>
    <li>Organic, adaptive forms responding to physical forces</li>
    <li>Efficient encoding of complex geometry using curve primitives</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Implementation</h2>
  <p>AdaptiveCAD provides a complete Python implementation including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Linear algebra core with quaternions and homogeneous coordinates</li>
    <li>Bézier and B-spline curve operations</li>
    <li>GUI playground with 3D visualization</li>
    <li>CAM toolpath generation and G-code export</li>
    <li>STL and STEP file import/export</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>